-- DICT-SEMANTICS §4.2 OD5/OD6 (obligation deferral, dedup): deduplicating two
-- call obligations must suppress the REPORT of a duplicate, never the CHECK. If
-- the dedup key collides across two DIFFERENT goals, the second goal is never
-- adjudicated and an unsatisfiable predicate ships.
--
-- REGRESSION GUARD FOR #1330 (call-obligation dedup skips the check), S0,
-- fixed by sprint/entailment-verdict. Written because the fix DELETED the
-- self-draining pin `test/must_fail_fixtures/1330-call-obligation-dedup-skips-
-- check/` per [G-PIN-DRAIN] and left the S0 with no guard: a pin asserts a bug
-- STILL REPRODUCES, so a fix deletes it and nothing replaces it unless someone
-- writes the positive row. This is that row. #1330 is also the named OD5
-- divergence in this gate's own NOT-YET-COVERED punch-list, so it is the first
-- §4.2 fixture the corpus has ever had.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived from §5 `(method)`, NOT captured). `println` is a
-- `Display`-dispatching prelude method. `println (1, 2)` raises the goal
-- `Display (Int, Int)`, which the prelude's tuple instance satisfies.
-- `println (Red, 3)` raises `Display (Color, Int)`, whose tuple instance in
-- turn requires `Display Color` -- and `data Color = Red` carries no
-- `deriving Display` and has no `impl Display Color`. §3's matching set for
-- `Display Color` is EMPTY. THE PROGRAM IS REJECTED, T-NO-IMPL, on check, run
-- AND build, with the located help `add 'deriving Display' to the 'Color'
-- type, or write an 'impl Display Color'.`
--
-- 🚨 THE TWO `println` GOALS ARE THE WHOLE FIXTURE, AND THEY MUST STAY TWO.
-- The body below is the drained pin's `main.mdk` VERBATIM, and per that pin's
-- own header both calls are `Display`-at-a-2-tuple occurrences, so their
-- call-channel obligations share a dedup key and the collision dropped the
-- first one's check. Deleting either line, or reshaping either tuple, breaks
-- the collision and leaves an ordinary missing-instance program -- inert here.
-- Five prelude-only lines is not minimalism for its own sake.
--
-- ⚠️ THE PIN'S `control.mdk` (the same two calls with `data Color = Red
-- deriving (Display)`, correctly ACCEPTED) IS DELIBERATELY NOT CARRIED OVER.
-- It is green at the pre-sprint arm AND at the fix, so it cannot regress-test
-- this fix; it would be an over-rejection guard, which is a different job. If a
-- future tightening of the dedup channel starts rejecting satisfiable
-- collisions, that control is the row to add, and this note is where to find it
-- (git history of test/must_fail_fixtures/1330-call-obligation-dedup-skips-
-- check/control.mdk).
--
-- MEASURED AT THE PRE-SPRINT ARM `264eb95d` (this tree, cold-built): `check`
-- exit 0 with an EMPTY `--json` diagnostics list, `build` exit 0, AND THE
-- SHIPPED BINARY DIED AT SIGNAL 139 (SEGFAULT) with empty stdout -- a null dict
-- reaching a call. Only `run` was loud (exit 1, E-PANIC `intToString: not an
-- Int`), and `run` is the one verb that does not ship.
--
-- ⚠️ NO `impl` BLOCKS AT ALL, so Section 4 derives no permutation pair; the
-- defect had no declaration-order face.
data Color = Red

main =
  let _ = println (Red, 3)
  println (1, 2)
